      ],
      "line": "Tally marks on the fold's gatepost, seven to a gate. The last week has only five, and then three.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        5,
        14
      ],
      "line": "A ram's collar on a nail, with no bell on it. The strap was not cut; it was bitten.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        24,
        11
      ],
      "line": "Tracks in the soft ground going over the hill: one set of hooves, and four sets of paws after them.",
      "page": true
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        12,
        4
      ],
      "line": "The lane north is worn to the stone. Whoever lives here walks it every night."
    },
    {
      "cell": [
        16,
        13
      ],
      "line": "A shepherd's crook lying where it was dropped, the crook end pointing at the hills.",
      "set_flag": "found:hollow_crook"
    }
  ],
  "people": [
    {
      "name": "Agna the shepherd",
      "unit": "town_farmer",
      "cell": [
        15,
        8
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 2,
      "chatter": [
        "Count them for me. I keep getting thirty-one and it should be forty.",
        "Wolves don't take a ram. Wolves take what's slow. Something took the ram."
      ],
      "talk": {
        "hello": [
          "You came over the hill? Then you came the way the wolves do. Did you see any?",
          "Travellers. Good. I have bread, and I have a wolf problem, and I'll swap one for the other."
        ],
        "again": "Still here? Then you can count sheep for me.",
        "ask": [
          {
            "q": "What's wrong with the fold?",
            "a": "Something comes down at night and takes one. The dogs won't go up there now. Look at the back of the fold, by the box, and you'll see what I mean."
          },
          {
            "q": "Where's the ram?",
            "a": "Gone after the bell. Old fool. He'd follow that bell into a gate."
          }
        ],
        "job": {
          "flag": "job:hollow_crook",
          "done_flag": "found:hollow_crook",
          "offer": "My crook. I dropped it running the night they came. It's somewhere on the green. Bring it back and I'll see you fed.",
          "done": "That's it. That's my crook. Here: bread for the road, and the herb I'd have used on my own leg.",
          "gold": 600,
          "item": "herbs"
        },
        "sells": [
          {
            "item": "bread",
            "restock": true
          },
          {
            "item": "herbs",
            "restock": true
          }
        ],
        "shop": "Bread from this morning. Herbs from the bank by the fold, before they started coming.",
        "sold": "Eat it while it's soft.",
        "bye": "Keep to the lane after dark."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Old Tallow",
      "unit": "town_elder",
      "cell": [
        10,
        5
      ],
      "facing": [
        0,
        1
      ],
      "wander": 1,
      "chatter": [
        "Sixty winters in the Hollow. This is the first one I've been afraid of the hill.",
        "Candles. That's what I make. You can't fight a wolf with a candle, but you can see one."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Pip, who wants to be a shepherd",
      "unit": "cabin_boy",
      "cell": [
        7,
        9
      ],
      "facing": [
        1,
        0
      ],
      "wander": 3,
      "chatter": [
        "I could fight a wolf. Mum says I couldn't fight a goose.",
        "Are you going up to the fold? Can I come? I'll stay behind you. Behind behind."
      ]
    }
  ],
